WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.388 --> 00:00:03.471
(lighthearted music)

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:06.459
- I had one kid say,

00:00:06.459 --> 00:00:07.499
"You're famous."

00:00:07.499 --> 00:00:08.332
And I said,

00:00:08.332 --> 00:00:09.165
"Oh, I'm not at all famous

00:00:09.165 --> 00:00:11.451
"compared to Michael Jackson."

00:00:11.451 --> 00:00:12.284
And the kid said,

00:00:12.284 --> 00:00:13.389
"Not that kind of famous.

00:00:13.389 --> 00:00:14.931
"Art famous."

00:00:14.931 --> 00:00:17.681
I found that kind of fascinating.

00:00:19.192 --> 00:00:20.173
I'm William Wegman,

00:00:20.173 --> 00:00:23.500
and most people know me
as The Dog Photographer.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.083
(upbeat music)

00:00:32.272 --> 00:00:33.721
I've been working with weimaraners

00:00:33.721 --> 00:00:35.221
for over 45 years.

00:00:36.847 --> 00:00:37.886
If I had a better voice,

00:00:37.886 --> 00:00:41.899
I'd compose a song about
all the dogs I've had.

00:00:41.899 --> 00:00:43.659
♫ First there was Man Ray

00:00:43.659 --> 00:00:46.080
♫ And then came Fay Wray

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:48.990
But I won't burden you with that.

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:50.910
Now I have two dogs:

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:54.069
Flo and her brother, Topper.

00:00:54.069 --> 00:00:55.497
And they're really…

00:00:55.497 --> 00:00:56.657
I love Flo.

00:00:56.657 --> 00:01:00.128
They're pretty amazing together.

00:01:00.128 --> 00:01:01.878
In my photographs,

00:01:01.878 --> 00:01:03.777
what I like people to see is that,

00:01:03.777 --> 00:01:05.294
yes, there is a dog.

00:01:05.294 --> 00:01:07.288
And yes, it's a weimaraner,

00:01:07.288 --> 00:01:09.736
but what has it become?

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:11.495
The dogs are always in a state

00:01:11.495 --> 00:01:12.977
of becoming something.

00:01:12.977 --> 00:01:15.644
They become characters, objects.

00:01:16.675 --> 00:01:18.046
When they're lying down,

00:01:18.046 --> 00:01:21.097
they're becoming landscapes.

00:01:21.097 --> 00:01:22.345
They let you do it.

00:01:22.345 --> 00:01:23.902
It's something special.

00:01:23.902 --> 00:01:25.545
It's something unique that happens

00:01:25.545 --> 00:01:27.505
only when we go to the studio,

00:01:27.505 --> 00:01:31.672
and there's an arena
established for this activity.

00:01:33.190 --> 00:01:35.663
I live in the Chelsea area of New York.

00:01:35.663 --> 00:01:38.371
I have this really great studio

00:01:38.371 --> 00:01:40.962
with tons of props stored in the basement.

00:01:40.962 --> 00:01:44.812
I'm gonna need to go
down and get those vests.

00:01:44.812 --> 00:01:48.441
Ball gowns and ugly stepsister outfits.

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:51.193
Doo-dads and crazy hats and wigs

00:01:51.193 --> 00:01:52.867
and all kinds of things.

00:01:52.867 --> 00:01:54.081
I'm seeing something on the floor.

00:01:54.081 --> 00:01:55.503
Oh, I gotta use that.

00:01:55.503 --> 00:01:58.015
We'll put that on the dog's head.

00:01:58.015 --> 00:02:00.462
Some people are alarmed when they see

00:02:00.462 --> 00:02:02.503
human hands attached to the arms.

00:02:02.503 --> 00:02:05.914
I like that because it's
almost like a mythology.

00:02:05.914 --> 00:02:08.005
You know, an Egyptian God with a bird head

00:02:08.005 --> 00:02:09.643
and human hands.

00:02:09.643 --> 00:02:10.792
Well, we really only need that,

00:02:10.792 --> 00:02:12.783
so just try that.

00:02:12.783 --> 00:02:15.465
I really need that energy of the lights,

00:02:15.465 --> 00:02:17.298
the camera, the focus.

00:02:19.974 --> 00:02:20.807
Good girl.

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:21.640
Stay.

00:02:23.753 --> 00:02:27.114
My work sort of jumped
out of the art world

00:02:27.114 --> 00:02:29.825
into everybody's world.

00:02:29.825 --> 00:02:33.086
I've seen my work appear on
the whole array of things:

00:02:33.086 --> 00:02:36.894
children's books, videos
for Sesame Street, films,

00:02:36.894 --> 00:02:38.561
all kinds of things.

00:02:39.814 --> 00:02:41.903
There was a time when I felt like I was

00:02:41.903 --> 00:02:43.134
nailed to the dog cross.

00:02:43.134 --> 00:02:45.114
I wanted to escape that.

00:02:45.114 --> 00:02:46.793
Now, I'm kind of comfortable with that,

00:02:46.793 --> 00:02:49.876
and I feel really lucky to have this.

00:02:52.985 --> 00:02:55.223
I think these might be my last two dogs.

00:02:55.223 --> 00:02:59.263
I'm in my 70’s, and I'll be
in my 80's when they're gone.

00:02:59.263 --> 00:03:00.993
Do I really want to burden my family

00:03:00.993 --> 00:03:02.246
with other dogs?

00:03:02.246 --> 00:03:03.079
I don't know.

00:03:03.079 --> 00:03:04.412
It's up to them.

00:03:05.273 --> 00:03:08.113
When I'm 95 and they want another dog?

00:03:08.113 --> 00:03:08.946
Okay, I'll get one.

00:03:08.946 --> 00:03:10.555
(laughs)

00:03:10.555 --> 00:03:11.697
Go for a walk?

00:03:11.697 --> 00:03:12.530
Good girl.

00:03:12.530 --> 00:03:13.577
Come on.

00:03:13.577 --> 00:03:14.410
Stay.

00:03:18.646 --> 00:03:22.229
(single high-pitched tone)

